8. The Cunt Variable

At this point the author wishes to disclose a possible methodological bias.

The author considers Matt Goodwin a cunt.

This variable has therefore been recorded.

However, Cunt Status is excluded from the principal model because it is neither necessary nor particularly analytically interesting.

The arguments can be tested without it.

Indeed, this is important.

A bad political argument does not become bad because its author is unpleasant.

It becomes bad when:

* its inference exceeds its evidence;
* counterexamples are ignored;
* correlation becomes causation;
* emotionally loaded framing substitutes for mechanism;
* predictions resist falsification;
* opponents are described differently from allies performing equivalent behaviour;
* or the conclusion appears suspiciously predetermined regardless of the data supplied.

If those defects exist, calling the author a cunt afterward is merely recreational.

